\uline{Proposition 1}. Let A be a small category, M a category stable under
finite products, $f\colon A\to M$ a functor, we assume A is a \xout{\illegible{1}} \uline{precon-}%
\uline{tractor}. Then f(A) generates a contractibility structure in M in
each of the following three cases:

a) A stable under finite products, and f commutes to these.

b) There exists a functor $f_{!}\colon A\hat{}\to M$ extend\xout{\illegible{1}}ing f, and commuting
to final object and binary products in $A\hat{}$of objects in A.

c) The functor f is fully faithful and strictly generating.

Of course, the validity of\inserted[typed]{the conclusion in either case} \xout{either} b) or c), for fixed A and
variable M and f, \uline{caracteri\unsure{z|s}es} the property for A of being a precon-%
tractor, and the same for a) if we assume beforehand that A is stable
under finite products. Thus we may view the proposition 1 as the most
comprehensive statement of \xout{what} the meaning of this property.

\uline{Proposition 2} Let A be a precontractor. Let $A\hat{}_{c}$ be the set of con-%
tractible \xout{elements}\inserted[typed]{objects} in $A\hat{}$ for \inserted[typed]{\xout{\illegible{1}}}the contractibility structure \xout{defined by}
generated by the subcategory A, $A\hat{}_{as}$ (resp. $A\hat{}_{totas}$ ) the set of
aspheric (resp. \over{t}{l}o\over{t}{c}ally aspheric\inserted{-- cf. p. 250})objects\xout{\illegible{1}} of $A\hat{}$, h the homotopy struc-%
ture on $A\hat{}$ associated to the contractibil\xout{\illegible{1}}ity structu\xout{\illegible{1}}re $A\hat{}_{c}$ i.e. genera-%
ted by the \xout{homotopy} intervals in $A\hat{}$ coming from A. As usual, $\underline{W}_{A}$ de-%
notes the set of weak equivalences in $A\hat{}$ - it is understood here that
